<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch04-the-derivative">
  <title>The Derivative</title>
  <shorttitle>The Derivative</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>A derivative is the limit of average rates of change over intervals shrinking to a point:</p><p><me>f\prime(a)=\lim_{h\to0}\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}.</me></p><p>When this finite limit exists, it gives the instantaneous rate of change and the tangent slope at that point. This chapter defines the derivative, develops its first formulas, and explains its use in local approximation and motion.</p></introduction>

